    mcp_interpreter_startup_12s_2026-09-14, 2, "closed-obsolete 2026-11-11 (opus perf lane): premise no longer holds. The proposed fix already landed one level down: main.spl keeps only `use app.mcp.main_dispatch.{dispatch_tool}` (module-level on purpose, seed JIT function-local-use segfault), and main_dispatch.spl imports only .main_lazy_json at top level, loading every handler family via function-local `use` inside its dispatch fn. Measured on seed bin/simple.exe sha256 8c7341592f4d47de (40739328 B, 2026-11-04), SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter SIMPLE_LOADER_TRACE=1 main.spl --probe: 84 modules loaded, inclusive load 277ms (top: io_runtime 277ms, process_ops 154ms; main_static_tools 18ms). Wall probe 2.07-2.37s peak RSS 102-108MB vs trivial fn main 1.0-1.9s 12-22MB on a loaded host; initialize-over-stdin TTFB 4-8s tracks probe/eof runs within host-load noise (probe 3.1-7.2s, eof-only 3.9-11.0s, init 4.0-8.3s same trials) - no MCP-specific eager load remains. Pinned by test/01_unit/app/mcp/handler_graph_lazy_boundary_spec.spl (3/3 pass). Residual cost is fixed seed interpreter startup, not MCP module graph."

